(footprint "T68-6_Flat_HandWound"
	(version 20240108)
	(generator "manual")
	(generator_version "9.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "T68-6 iron powder toroid (Micrometals/Amidon mix 6, yellow, A_L = 4.7 nH/N^2 = 47 microH per 100 turns-squared -- catalogs typically list the latter form; use 4.7 in the N = sqrt(L_nH / A_L) formula), hand-wound, laying flat on PCB with axis perpendicular to board. Both leads exit on the same radial side; outer lead sits just outside the OD (17.53 mm) at pad 1 (0, -10); inner lead sits inside the ID hole (9.40 mm) at pad 2 (0, -2.5). Pitch center-to-center 7.5 mm. Suits 10-13 turn 24 AWG magnet wire winding (e.g. 12 T for 20 m LPF nominal 677 nH). Silk shows OD and ID circles. Four 3.1 mm NPTH zip-tie holes in two tie groups: each tie has one hole just inside the ID (at X=+-2.9, Y=0) and one hole just outside the OD (at X=+-9.9, Y=0), with the tie wrapping across the donut wall on that side.  Tie direction = X axis, 90 deg from the wire-pad axis (Y).  Two ties on opposite sides of the toroid clamp it down firmly without crossing the ID center.  Hole positions: inside = +-(ID/2 - hole_radius - 0.3 mm margin) = +-2.9; outside = +-(OD/2 + 24AWG + 0.5 mm margin) = +-9.9.  Courtyard sized to cover the tie holes.")
	(tags "toroid iron powder t68-6 amidon micrometals hand wound flat")
